<title>BELGIUM: Ciampi pledged further EMU moves if needed - source.</title>
<headline>Ciampi pledged further EMU moves if needed - source.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi told fellow European Union ministers on Monday that Italy would take further measures to qualify for economic and monetary union (EMU) if needed, an EU source said.</p>
<p>&quot;If needed to respect the criteria, we will take other measures,&quot; Ciampi was quoted as saying during a discussion of Italy's EMU convergence programme.</p>
</text>
